        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l03-logaritmo",
      "title": "Función logarítmica de base a y propiedades",
      "summary": "logₐ x como inversa de aˣ, propiedades, cambio de base, ecuaciones y derivada.",
      "minutes": 22,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "expression": "y = logₐ x   ⇔   aʸ = x        (a > 0, a ≠ 1, x > 0)",
          "caption": "Definición: el logaritmo es un exponente"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "concepto",
          "text": "logₐ x pregunta: “¿a qué exponente hay que elevar a para obtener x?”. log₂ 8 = 3 porque 2³ = 8. Es la inversa de aˣ, por eso su gráfica es el reflejo de aˣ en y = x.",
          "title": "En palabras"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Propiedad",
            "Fórmula",
            "Ejemplo"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Producto",
              "logₐ(MN) = logₐ M + logₐ N",
              "log₂ 32 = log₂ 4 + log₂ 8 = 2 + 3"
            ],
            [
              "Cociente",
              "logₐ(M/N) = logₐ M − logₐ N",
              "log₃(81/9) = 4 − 2"
            ],
            [
              "Potencia",
              "logₐ(Mᵖ) = p·logₐ M",
              "log₁₀ 1000 = 3·log₁₀ 10"
            ],
            [
              "Valores clave",
              "logₐ 1 = 0;  logₐ a = 1",
              "ln 1 = 0, ln e = 1"
            ],
            [
              "Inversas",
              "logₐ(aˣ) = x;  a^(logₐ x) = x",
              "10^(log 7) = 7"
            ],
            [
              "Cambio de base",
              "logₐ x = ln x / ln a",
              "log₂ 10 = ln 10/ln 2 ≈ 3,3219"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "importante",
          "text": "No existen “propiedades” para logₐ(M + N) ni para (logₐ M)·(logₐ N). Error típico: log(x + 3) ≠ log x + log 3.",
          "title": "Lo que NO se puede"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Propiedad de la gráfica",
            "a > 1",
            "0 < a < 1"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Dominio / rango",
              "(0, ∞) / ℝ",
              "(0, ∞) / ℝ"
            ],
            [
              "Monotonía",
              "Creciente",
              "Decreciente"
            ],
            [
              "Asíntota vertical",
              "x = 0 (→ −∞)",
              "x = 0 (→ +∞)"
            ],
            [
              "Corte con x",
              "(1, 0)",
              "(1, 0)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ecuaciones exponenciales y logarítmicas"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "ejemplo",
          "text": "2ˣ = 10 → aplico ln: x ln 2 = ln 10 → **x = ln 10/ln 2 ≈ 3,32**.",
          "title": "Ejemplo 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "ejemplo",
          "text": "log₃(x − 1) + log₃(x + 1) = 1 → log₃(x² − 1) = 1 → x² − 1 = 3 → x = ±2.\nComo x − 1 > 0, se descarta −2: **x = 2**. Siempre verifica el dominio.",
          "title": "Ejemplo 2"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "ejemplo",
          "text": "e^(2x) − 5eˣ + 6 = 0: con u = eˣ, u² − 5u + 6 = 0 → u = 2 o u = 3 → **x = ln 2 o x = ln 3**.",
          "title": "Ejemplo 3: cambio de variable"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Derivada"
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "expression": "d/dx logₐ x = 1/(x·ln a)        d/dx logₐ u = u′/(u·ln a)        d/dx ln|u| = u′/u"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "ejemplo",
          "text": "d/dx log₁₀(x² + 1) = 2x/[(x² + 1) ln 10]\nd/dx log₂(sen x) = cos x/(sen x·ln 2) = cot x/ln 2\nd/dx ln(x³ − 4x) = (3x² − 4)/(x³ − 4x)\nd/dx ln √(x² + 1) = ½·2x/(x² + 1) = x/(x² + 1) (primero baja el exponente con la propiedad).",
          "title": "Ejemplos"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "ingenieria",
          "text": "Escalas logarítmicas: nivel sonoro β = 10·log₁₀(I/I₀) dB; pH = −log₁₀[H⁺]; magnitud de sismos. Útiles cuando una cantidad varía en muchos órdenes de magnitud."
        },
        {
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "log₅ 125 =",
          "options": [
            "3",
            "25",
            "5",
            "1/3"
          ],
          "correct": 0,
          "explanation": "5³ = 125."
        },
        {
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "log₂ 6 − log₂ 3 =",
          "options": [
            "log₂ 3",
            "1",
            "2",
            "log₂ 18"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "log₂(6/3) = log₂ 2."
        },
        {
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "d/dx log₃ x =",
          "options": [
            "1/x",
            "1/(x ln 3)",
            "ln 3/x",
            "3/x"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "1/(x ln a)."
        },
        {
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "Solución de 3ˣ = 20:",
          "options": [
            "20/3",
            "ln 20/ln 3",
            "ln 3/ln 20",
            "log 20 − log 3"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "Aplicar ln."
        },
        {
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "Dominio de log(x − 4):",
          "options": [
            "ℝ",
            "(4, ∞)",
            "[4, ∞)",
            "(0, ∞)"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "x − 4 > 0."
        },
        {
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "log(x + 3) es igual a:",
          "options": [
            "log x + log 3",
            "log x · log 3",
            "No se simplifica",
            "3 log x"
